// CRYPT SHIFT — RAISE THE DEAD — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CRYPT SHIFT as a horror big-room anthem — THE BANGER of the three crypt remixes. A game
// alternate of crypt, selectable from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk.
// Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// The A–C–B hook is a festival riff already — a dotted crotchet, a crotchet, a dotted
// crotchet — so the drops play it at its own speed on an electric grand in octaves, a
// plain square doubling it and an ice bell an octave up, over a pumping supersaw, an
// off-beat MONSTER bass, four on the floor and a church bell on every one. Drop one is
// the A phrase twice; the drop after the choir is the A phrase and the climbing
// D–C–Bm–E passage from bars 29–32; the breakdown plays the hook at half speed over the
// descending Am–G–F–E of bars 37–40, and the build climbs that passage at its own speed.
// Drop two jumps a whole step to B minor with a screaming lead an octave over the hook,
// then switches to half time; the B phrase builds back down to A minor. Before each
// big drop a growled "raise the dead" — the Announcer preset on the titan throat, its
// phrase compiled into this song (voiceParams) — lands its last word on the one.
// 
//   1–4    intro — ice-bell hook, choir, heartbeat kick (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    build — the hook on the grand, snare 2s→4s→8s→16s, riser, the tag
//   9–16   DROP ONE — the A phrase twice
//   17–24  GHOST CHOIR — half-time, the middle-eight tune sung, bell replies
//   25–32  drop — the A phrase, then the climb (Dm C Bm E)
//   33–36  breakdown — the hook at half speed on the grand, choir, no drums
//   37–40  build — the descending passage at its own speed, roll, riser
//   41–56  DROP TWO — B minor, screaming lead an octave up
//   57–60  half-time switch — the hook at half speed, still B minor
//   61–64  build — the B phrase back in A minor
//   65–72  GHOST CHOIR two — darker, the grand answering the choir
//   73–80  LAST DROP — everything; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// WEATHER SYNC: the crypt eclipse runs on the heard song beat (CRYPT_WEATHER_TIMING,
// a 192-beat / 48-bar cycle counted from bar 1, whatever the tempo). Bars 17–24 and
// 65–72 — beats 64–96 of the first and second cycle — are the choir: clouds gather on
// the last beats of bars 16 and 64, and the drops at 25 and 73 land as they clear. The
// loop (5–80) ends on cycle beat 128, after the clouds have gone.
// 
// 80 bars at 128. Written by work/local/_crypt-remix-raise-the-dead.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): stutter rolls on beat 3 of 8 and 40; the Ghost Choir swells in over its first two bars (17, 65).
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
